      "scope": "pagination-absent-proven-to-29k-rows",
      "reason": "No pagination is documented anywhere for the Report API across every source checked: both first-party API-doc copies, all 59 release notes, all 34 Reports-folder documentation articles, and both third-party integration guides. That documented negative has now been CONFIRMED EMPIRICALLY rather than left unproven. PROBED AND DECIDED NEGATIVE AT VOLUME, 2026-08-25 (RealityProbe amendment round 1, packages/Integration/connectors-registry/elevate/runs/connector-elevate-1787634178034-39f0b3cc/output/elevate-read-probe.mjs). One unfiltered POST for resource=''productRegistration'' returned 29,003 rows. The SAME query partitioned into 15 consecutive non-overlapping yearly windows (2013..2027) summed to EXACTLY 29,003 — every window HTTP 200 (2013:0, 2014:254, 2015:46, 2016:208, 2017:314, 2018:72, 2019:558, 2020:309, 2021:5608, 2022:8458, 2023:12334, 2024:283, 2025:296, 2026:263, 2027:0). windowedSum == unfilteredCount => NO silent cap at 29k rows. Corroborated independently on all five probed resources by the door''s own total: response.count == response.items.length on earnedCredit 3395/3395, product 1985/1985, user 6818/6818, accountingCode 7/7, productRegistration 29003/29003. Five parameters were tried in the request envelope (limit, offset, page, per_page, page_size) and NONE changed the row count — the envelope exposes no pagination control at all, so there is nothing to declare. The GrowthZone silent-one-page-cap defect class does NOT apply to this vendor at this volume. NOT a claim of unlimited results: 29,003 rows is the ceiling actually PROBED; above it, behaviour is unmeasured, which is exactly why the date-window chunking obligation below stays in force. METHOD CAVEAT (recorded so this is never re-derived unsoundly): an earlier pass of this same adapter at 1.1s pacing produced a FALSE cap-negative (windowedSum 28,161 < 29,003) purely because its last 4 windows came back 429 rate-limited and were counted as 0. That pass was discarded and the probe re-paced to 3.4s. A sum-vs-unfiltered comparison is sound ONLY when every window returns HTTP 200 — otherwise a rate limit masquerades as missing data and a healthy API is condemned as silently truncating.",
      "consequence": "The door returns the complete result set for a query in one response, and completeness is verifiable per call: the connector MUST compare response.count against the length of response.items on EVERY read and raise a FetchWarning when they diverge — that comparison is the silent-truncation tripwire, and it is the only protection that survives above the 29,003-row volume actually probed. Because there is no page/offset/cursor control to fall back on, bulk extraction above that volume is bounded by DATE WINDOWS via the filters envelope (transaction_at / modified_at date-range shortcut), not by pages. Do not add a pagination parameter: five were tried and none is honoured."
