  "paginationProvenNegative": "Pagination is documented NOWHERE for this API: no page/offset/cursor parameter and no response envelope in either first-party API-doc copy, zero genuine hits across all 59 release notes (the 5 \"pagination\" hits are all admin-UI screens), none in the Reports-folder articles, none in either third-party guide. SupportsPagination=false is a PROVEN negative, not an unchecked default; bulk extraction is bounded by DATE WINDOWS via the filters envelope. PROBED AND DECIDED NEGATIVE AT VOLUME, 2026-08-25 (RealityProbe amendment round 1, packages/Integration/connectors-registry/elevate/runs/connector-elevate-1787634178034-39f0b3cc/output/elevate-read-probe.mjs). One unfiltered POST for resource=''productRegistration'' returned 29,003 rows. The SAME query partitioned into 15 consecutive non-overlapping yearly windows (2013..2027) summed to EXACTLY 29,003 — every window HTTP 200 (2013:0, 2014:254, 2015:46, 2016:208, 2017:314, 2018:72, 2019:558, 2020:309, 2021:5608, 2022:8458, 2023:12334, 2024:283, 2025:296, 2026:263, 2027:0). windowedSum == unfilteredCount => NO silent cap at 29k rows. Corroborated independently on all five probed resources by the door''s own total: response.count == response.items.length on earnedCredit 3395/3395, product 1985/1985, user 6818/6818, accountingCode 7/7, productRegistration 29003/29003. Five parameters were tried in the request envelope (limit, offset, page, per_page, page_size) and NONE changed the row count — the envelope exposes no pagination control at all, so there is nothing to declare. The GrowthZone silent-one-page-cap defect class does NOT apply to this vendor at this volume. NOT a claim of unlimited results: 29,003 rows is the ceiling actually PROBED; above it, behaviour is unmeasured, which is exactly why the date-window chunking obligation below stays in force. METHOD CAVEAT (recorded so this is never re-derived unsoundly): an earlier pass of this same adapter at 1.1s pacing produced a FALSE cap-negative (windowedSum 28,161 < 29,003) purely because its last 4 windows came back 429 rate-limited and were counted as 0. That pass was discarded and the probe re-paced to 3.4s. A sum-vs-unfiltered comparison is sound ONLY when every window returns HTTP 200 — otherwise a rate limit masquerades as missing data and a healthy API is condemned as silently truncating.",
